WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.100
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.167
You're here. You made it.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.667
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.267
You guys, this is very exciting.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:10.901
Tomorrow is the annual lighting

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.968
of the Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.567
Yes.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:19.100
The Christmas tree lighting
is kind of like prom night.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.534
There's tons of buildup and
then it's over in one second.

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:26.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:29.367
I heard that the tree will be
topped by a giant star

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.234
that has 3 million crystals.

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:32.868
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:36.834
I love that New York locks up
the deodorant at CVS and then

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.000
leaves 3 million crystals
in the middle of the street.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:43.901
[ Applause ]

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:46.767
Meanwhile, I saw that the tree
lighting ceremony could actually

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.267
be affected by heavy rain

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:51.634
and wind gusts up to
50 miles an hour.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.267
[ Audience ohs ]

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.934
You know earlier when I said
I was excited for

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.267
the tree lighting, I didn't
mean it, but now I am.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:01:00.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.734
Yeah, that's where you want to
be during a massive storm.

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:06.234
Under an 80-foot tree with a
9-foot star and no root system.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.033
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.501
Suddenly Mario Lopez is yelling,
"Timber!"

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.834
Don't worry, if the weather gets
really bad, NBC has a plan.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.634
They're just going to air
last year's tree lighting

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.534
because it looks the same.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:22.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:25.133
The exact same.

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:31.334
That's right, tomorrow is
the Christmas tree lighting

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.033
in Rockefeller Center,
but tonight we thought

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.601
we'd also do something special.

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:35.801
We've never done this before.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.100
Tonight we present to you,

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.601
the first annual lighting
of the beard!

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:42.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.667
Roots, can I get
some holiday music?

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:48.501
And let's bring down the lights
for a second here.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.400
♪♪

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.834
Alright, let's count it down.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:55.334
3, 2, 1.

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:56.634
Happy holidays.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:02:01.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.567
Thank you very much.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.400
-The lighting of the beard
is brought to you

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.934
by Terry's Steaks.
Terry's Steaks -- makes you say,

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.868
"Mmm, that kinda tastes
like beef!"

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:10.767
-There you go.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.200
Here's some good news.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.734
Today is Giving Tuesday.

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:18.367
[ Audience ohs ]
Yeah.

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.267
That's right.
[ Applause ]

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:23.501
It's a day of generosity
when millions of people give

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:26.667
to their favorite charities
or struggling organizations.

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:29.234
Which explains why Twitter
was trending all day.

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:30.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.934
That's right,
today is Giving Tuesday.

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:35.033
I love giving, especially
on Giving Tuesday,

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:37.067
but of course there's one thing
I'm not going to give.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.033
-Really? What's that?

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.701
-It's just something
I'm never going to give.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:44.033
-Well, what is it?

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:48.400
-I, Jimmy Fallon, am never...

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.667
[ Note plays ]

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:54.801
♪ Gonna give you up,
never gonna let you down ♪

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:58.501
♪ Never gonna run around
and desert you ♪

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.834
You got Rick Roll'd.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.868
-That Rick Roll was brought
to you by Terry's Steaks.

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:05.767
Terry's Steaks -- makes you say,

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:07.901
"Mmm, that kinda tastes
like beef!"

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:11.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.901
-People were talking about this.

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:15.601
Last year, several Oscar
categories were cut

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:18.567
from the live telecast,
and everyone was outraged.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.400
So the Academy just announced
that this year,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.200
all 23 Oscar categories
will be presented live.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:27.601
That's right.

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:29.133
That should be fun.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.634
All the length of a Marvel movie
with none of the excitement.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:33.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:36.901
Hey, some big sports news.
Today the U.S. beat Iran 1-0

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:39.667
to advance to the next round of
the World Cup.

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:43.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes!

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:44.434
U.S.A.!

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:48.167
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:49.634
I just hope this doesn't ruin

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:51.300
our incredible friendship
with Iran.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.167
Yeah, we're on to
the next round.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:57.267
Americans haven't been
this fired up about soccer

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.200
since we remembered
it existed last week.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:04.434
When asked how they beat Iran,
the U.S. coach said,

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:07.300
"We found their secret game plan
in a box at Mar-a-Lago."

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:13.467
That's right, the second week of
the World Cup started today.

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:15.234
The games have been so fun
to watch that we've actually

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:17.567
started playing a little soccer
around the office.

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:18.701
Tariq, you ready for this?

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:20.100
-Yeah, man, pass it to me.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.067
-Alright. Here we go, bud.

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:23.234
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:28.100
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪
-Ooh!

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.834
[ Alarm blares ]
-Murder robot activated.

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:33.334
-Does anyone know
the Heimlich maneuver?

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:35.701
[ Audience ohs ]

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:42.300
He's still choking!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.701
Oh, nice.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.801
[ Alarm blares ]
-Dance robot activated.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:50.400
-2, 1.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.501
-Wow! It's fun.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:04.534
Well, get this, a temple
in Thailand dismissed

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:08.467
all their monks because they
just tested positive for meth.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:13.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:15.634
Which explains the new hit show
in Thailand,

00:05:15.634 --> 00:05:16.701
"Breaking Buddhist."

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:18.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:21.133
Guys, finally, it is Tuesday.
it is time for "WeTweet"!

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:22.133
Here we go.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:25.167
-♪ WeTweet ♪

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.667
♪ WeTweet ♪

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:30.033
-Welcome to "WeTweet."

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:32.400
This is where we, as a group,

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.968
decide something that we should
post on Twitter.

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:36.767
I'm going to show you
five different tweets.

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:38.200
We're all going to vote on

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.367
whether you like
each one or not.

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:41.133
You all have voting clickers
at your seats.

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:42.501
You see them there.

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:43.968
You can vote for all of them,
if you like.

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:46.167
You can vote for none of them.
Whatever you want.

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:47.567
We're going to see
the results live.

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:48.801
Higgins, Roots,
you have clickers?

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:50.634
-Got it.
-Alright. Very good.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:53.834
Whichever gets the most likes,
we're gonna tweet it out,

00:05:53.834 --> 00:05:56.601
so you can all like it
and wetweet it.

00:05:56.601 --> 00:05:58.601
[ Laughs ]
It's a shared experience.

00:05:58.601 --> 00:05:59.901
Alright, guys,
you ready for this?

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:03.901
-[ Cheers ]
-Alright.

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:05.601
And be kind. It's the holidays.

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:07.868
Okay, here we go.
The first tweet is...

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:15.734
-Wow.
-Yeah, just dead silence.

00:06:15.734 --> 00:06:17.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:20.234
Not even a titter.
-Not even a titter.

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.901
-Not even a titter for Twitter.
-Not even a golf applause.

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.234
-Nothing on that one. Alright.

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:26.234
I think the votes are
probably in on this one.

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:28.601
Let's see the results.

00:06:28.601 --> 00:06:29.601
Yeah.
-Whoa!

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.267
[ Sad tuba ]

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:34.467
Wow! 132.

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:36.300
-Not everyone even voted on
that.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.901
-No. They said, "We're good.
No thanks."

00:06:38.901 --> 00:06:40.701
-"Jimmy, we're here for
the commercial breaks."

00:06:40.701 --> 00:06:42.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.968
-Want more Terry's Steaks.
-This next one says...

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:50.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:55.367
It's all -- Every page.

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:57.934
Some weird -- Yeah.
-Neon blue.

00:06:57.934 --> 00:06:59.901
-Smurf.
-Windex.

00:06:59.901 --> 00:07:02.000
-Yeah, Windex.
Smurf, whatever they want.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.067
Yeah, here we go.

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:04.267
Let's see the results
on this one.

00:07:04.267 --> 00:07:05.634
I think this one
will fare better.

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:06.667
Alright. Not bad.

00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:08.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:10.868
-112.
-Yeah.

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:12.267
-Tough crowd. Very honest.

00:07:12.267 --> 00:07:14.200
Very honest.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.667
It doesn't really matter,
I should also let you know.

00:07:16.667 --> 00:07:17.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.934 --> 00:07:19.100
This next one here says...

00:07:21.901 --> 00:07:23.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.501 --> 00:07:25.767
-Come on.
-I don't want to go there.

00:07:25.767 --> 00:07:27.934
It's too much work.

00:07:27.934 --> 00:07:30.400
-How is Jim?
-Oh, he's doing well.

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:33.400
Let's see the results here.

00:07:34.334 --> 00:07:35.901
-Whoa!

00:07:35.901 --> 00:07:37.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:37.868 --> 00:07:39.067
-I knew that.

00:07:39.067 --> 00:07:41.434
I appreciate that.
So they do work.

00:07:41.434 --> 00:07:44.167
The clickers do work.
Alright, that's real.

00:07:44.167 --> 00:07:46.100
I love this. Alright. Fun.
This is good.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.100
That might be --
-That might be the winner, 171.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.434
-I think it definitely is
going to be the winner.

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:51.033
Alright, let's see.
The next one says...

00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:56.434
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:58.701
Would you like a black one?
-Please.

00:07:58.701 --> 00:08:01.000
Do you have a blue one?
-We don't have black markers.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.834
-What do you have?
-We have blue.

00:08:02.834 --> 00:08:05.200
-I'm good.
-Okay.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.834
Let's see the results
on this one.

00:08:08.234 --> 00:08:09.667
Yeah. Wow.

00:08:09.667 --> 00:08:11.267
[ Crowd booing ]

00:08:11.267 --> 00:08:13.601
-[ Sad tuba ]
-No, you can't boo. No, stop.

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:16.901
Don't play that. Don't boo.
They're all fun.

00:08:16.901 --> 00:08:19.767
-Well, that tweet was
the Pepsi of this round.

00:08:19.767 --> 00:08:21.467
-Yeah.

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:22.934
-Wow!

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:24.267
-Alright. This last one says...

00:08:27.901 --> 00:08:29.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.968 --> 00:08:33.100
-Oh, wow!

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:35.067
-This is just
my favorite sweater.

00:08:35.067 --> 00:08:36.834
How dare you?

00:08:36.834 --> 00:08:39.534
Alright, here we go.
Let's see the results.

00:08:40.934 --> 00:08:43.300
-Oh!
-That's the winner right there,
everybody.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:46.133
By one vote.
Ugly Christmas sweater.

00:08:46.133 --> 00:08:47.834
I'm going to post this
during the commercial break.

00:08:47.834 --> 00:08:49.667
If you see it on your feed,
give it a like,

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:51.133
give it a wetweet, and enjoy.

